[Music]  Sean Mannion and his father have always  been close but sean is preparing to  leave their home village of Ross Moke  and the country patty Mannion has  decided not to see his son off at the  airport Sean is leaving this remote  western edge of Ireland for big-city  life on the other side of the Atlantic  to Boston a traditional magnet for Irish  immigrants Sean is starting to miss Ross  smoked even before he's left I love Ross  smoke and I love living in Ireland and  everything all my friends and family  obviously here like and I play football  and soccer and whatnot but it's no life  for a young lad you can't save moving  and even if you do get ahead of yourself  something happens to the care or  something you know something goes in the  car this has to be done there there's  always something that you just can't get  back a little bit of head Shan trained  as a plumber and welder but was able to  find a permanent job after qualifying  instead he's been working on his  father's small farm and doing odd jobs  but often he's left to make ends meet on  welfare checks he won't be the first in  his family to emigrate a number of his  relatives already live in Boston his own  parents spent 20 years there but never  forgot where home was  I think the dark Easter Coast the docks  the people that's where you're born when  you're born or something back in your  mind all the time that that you want to  come back everybody want to come back  some time which half them don't never  makes it Sean will no doubt miss his  mom's freshly baked bread the family has  gathered the day before his departure  Sean is reluctant to leave but like many  other young men he's frustrated by a  lack of prospects in iron  despite his qualifications last year  alone almost 90,000 left the country  shun also pops over to the neighboring  village to say goodbye to some friends  and to get a haircut just tend to look  nice for all the Yankee girls when I get  over there  Shaun is glad that his friend Martin  will also be moving to Boston soon he's  a trained bricklayer and likewise mostly  unemployed  Lisa O'Toole has known the two of them  since school days she's sad to see so  many young people leaving Ireland seven  out of ten I've gone yeah and they're  like they've had their like second or  third year visa in Australia or America  and that's obsessed and they'll come  home Christmas every second year or  something because it kind of bored him  home any other time a number of homes in  raw smoke are already vacant and pupil  numbers at the primary school are  falling due to the low birthrate Shaun  spends his last evening in one of the  villages last remaining pubs he's talked  often with a proprietor about his plans  to emigrate Christopher is a local  history buff and says that 10,000 people  left for the US alone over the past 100  years but he says the current wave of  emigration seems bigger than any before  well they can come back whenever they  please but 15 years before you're you're  on a kind of an even keel again there's  a big hole in the ship and it's going to  take a long time to bail it out Ireland  is still struggling to recover from a  recession and there's little sign here  in raw smoke of a resurgent Celtic Tiger  a former boss of Shaun's has had to  massively downsize operations model my  baldies I used to have port  staff now I just have to and I don't  even have enough work for them moment to  myself really know but I'm just from  here  fooled and Shawn fold unbelievable views  Shaun is planning to be gone for ten  years he's packed modestly a few pairs  of pants and soccer jerseys but with no  shortage of optimism I work trying to  put two of my cousin's in case was one  of them might not be stacking right away  so hopefully I'll be working Monday  after I learn the Mannion's are  confident their only son will make it in  Boston he hopes to earn over two  thousand dollars a week  Shawn's plans to wire some of that money  back home our little consolation for his  family of course they hope he'll return  at some point in the future to that  place where the heart is home in County  Galway  [Music]

